WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.179
A precious psalm this is, and many of us are familiar with this psalm, and we've looked

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:11.779
at it various times throughout the years, and we've been blessed by it.

00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:16.659
And I really just want to start dealing with the psalm in verse number 7 this evening.

00:00:16.659 --> 00:00:20.899
I'm going to read the verses, we'll get right into the message.

00:00:20.899 --> 00:00:23.979
Psalm 19, beginning in verse number 7.

00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:29.840
The Bible says this, the law of the Lord is perfect, converting the soul.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.020
The testimony of the Lord is sure, making wise the simple.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:37.740
The statutes of the Lord are right, rejoicing the heart.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.279
The commandment of the Lord is pure, enlightening the eyes.

00:00:42.279 --> 00:00:45.919
The fear of the Lord is clean, enduring forever.

00:00:45.919 --> 00:00:51.159
The judgments of the Lord are true and righteous altogether.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:55.080
More to be desired are they than gold.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.560
Notice what it says, yea, than much fine gold.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.720
Sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:11.260
Moreover by them is thy servant warned, and in keeping of them there is great reward.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:13.720
Who can understand his errors?

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.360
Cleanse thou me from secret faults.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.559
Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous sins.

00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:25.080
Let them not have dominion over me.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:30.800
Then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:37.519
Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable in thy sight, O

00:01:37.519 --> 00:01:41.760
Lord, my strength and my Redeemer.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.160
As we look at this portion of scripture this evening, I've simply titled the message

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.720
The Law of the Lord, and we'll look at these verses of scripture, but we understand as

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.400
a Bible-believing church, we talk much about the Bible.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:59.400
In fact, we would say as Baptists that we declare that the Bible is the sole authority

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.839
for faith and practice.

00:02:01.839 --> 00:02:06.800
We stand upon that, and we rejoice in the truth that we have a Bible.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.839
In fact, we sing songs about the Bible.

00:02:09.839 --> 00:02:13.800
And one of the little songs that we sing in Sunday school in junior church, and we've

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:19.559
taught it to our grandchildren, the B-I-B-L-E, yes, that's the book for me.

00:02:19.559 --> 00:02:20.559
Amen?

00:02:20.559 --> 00:02:22.320
Aren't you thankful to have a Bible?

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:28.000
I stand alone on the word of God, the B-I-B-L-E, and I'm thankful.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.639
Wonderful words of life, sing them over again to me, and we think about these wonderful

00:02:32.639 --> 00:02:39.320
songs and just the fact that we have a Bible, and we're thankful, and we stand up and we

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.320
declare.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.720
It is the sole authority for our faith and practice.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.240
And I would say all these things are good, and right, and proper.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:53.000
However, I believe this evening that the reality is that you can go to a Bible-believing

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.919
church, claim to be a Baptist, sing songs about the Bible, and yet spend very little

00:02:59.919 --> 00:03:07.160
time reading, studying, and applying the word of God personally in your life.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.880
I'm thankful we have the right Bible.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.559
I'm thankful we have a Bible.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:14.279
I'm thankful that we can sing about, preach about, talk about the Bible.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:19.479
And I want you to understand that it's absolutely imperative that the word of God that we say

00:03:19.479 --> 00:03:24.759
that we believe, that we stand upon, that we sing about, that we would declare to others

00:03:24.759 --> 00:03:29.880
maybe that would talk about various things with regard to tradition and other things.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.639
No, no, no, the Bible, the Bible, the Bible.

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:36.679
But we need to be careful that the Bible doesn't just become something that we talk about and

00:03:36.679 --> 00:03:43.919
not something that we spend time just feasting upon the manna of God's word.

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:47.919
We find that the psalmist did not have the complete revelation of God.

00:03:47.919 --> 00:03:50.240
How many of you are thankful to have the whole Bible this evening?

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.240
Amen.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.559
I mean, we don't just have a part of it.

00:03:52.559 --> 00:03:54.639
We don't just have sections of it.

00:03:54.639 --> 00:03:56.600
We don't just have a New Testament.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.119
You know, we send Bibles all around the world with Beacon of Truth Baptist Ministries.

00:04:01.119 --> 00:04:05.240
And at times, some of those places, they only get John.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.600
Maybe sometimes they get Romans.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.940
Maybe John and Romans.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.679
Sometimes they just get a New Testament.

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:13.960
But we have the whole canon of Scripture, the whole Bible.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.600
What a blessing.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:20.839
And we think about the truth that the psalmist did not have the complete revelation of God.

00:04:20.839 --> 00:04:28.359
And yet we understand that the psalmist loved the Bible, loved the word of God.

00:04:28.359 --> 00:04:33.480
And we find that as you study through the Psalms that his love for the Scriptures is

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.880
clearly understood.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.640
It's declared plainly.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.540
But then we understand that not only, listen, it's fine for us to say, I love the Bible.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.880
But if you love the Bible, then you're going to meditate upon it.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.640
You're going to spend time with God's word.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.440
You're going to apply God's word.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:53.119
And you're going to understand that there is evidence of your love for the word of God.

00:04:53.119 --> 00:04:57.679
And we find that the psalmist loved the word of God, which resulted in reading, memorizing,

00:04:57.679 --> 00:05:01.600
declaring, and applying the Scriptures in his own life.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:05.839
And for us this evening, as we look at this portion of Scripture, I hope, again, a familiar

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:10.760
passage, but one in which we'll look afresh this evening and trust God to give us something

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.399
that would help us.

00:05:12.399 --> 00:05:15.679
If you're taking notes, number one, the word of God is described.

00:05:15.679 --> 00:05:21.140
Beginning in verse number seven and down through verse number nine, God gives us some description

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.399
